SALT Compiler README
--------------------

The SALT compiler is a program that translates temporal specifications
in the SALT language into LTL and TLTL formulae.

(C) 2006 Jonathan Streit and contributors.
The SALT compiler comes with ABSOLUTELY NO WARRANTY.
It is released under the GNU GPL as free software, and you are welcome 
to redistribute it under certain conditions. See the file LICENSE 
for details. The file AUTHORS contains a full list of developers and
contributors.

The SALT compiler can be downloaded from http://salt.in.tum.de as
binary or source. The website also provides further information and a 
web interface to the compiler. The authors can be contacted at 
salt _AT_ mailbroy.informatik.tu-muenchen.de. Feedback is greatly
appreciated.

See the manual for information on how to install and use the SALT
compiler as well as for a tutorial and reference to the SALT language.
If you want to build the compiler from source (only necessary
if you want to modify it), use the ANT-Buildfile build.xml included
in the source distribution.